[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2670930415","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103055#issuecomment-2670930415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103055","id":2670930415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fMynv","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T09:30:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T10:01:03Z","body":"I dont think this is fully true with that it takes 2 steps.\r\n\r\nIf you place anything inside the physics queue it is consumed on the next physics sync and will be part of the updated query physics space.\r\n\r\nThat I mentioned in one of the issues that it is only ready after the second physics sync was because the user was using a RayCast node that, without force update, operates on delayed old data. If you do physics queries with the space directly you do not have that delay.\r\n\r\nI wouldn't mention a \"hard\" number anyway. How the tree adds or removes nodes, how the deferred queue gets flushed, and how physics decides to do steps are not in sync at all. The physics loop is way to unreliable. Instead, I would only mentioned that those nodes create their physics objects after joining the tree and require waiting for physics synchronisation. The RayCast nodes might need additional documentation for all their node related quirks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2670930415/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2741726282","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103055#issuecomment-2741726282","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103055","id":2741726282,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ja2xK","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T21:36:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T21:36:45Z","body":"While it's nice to document this (I have noticed it myself), it may be best to find a way to solve this oddity. A signal, a method to check for this, or something similar.","author_assoc